Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 09:10:28 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] debug: ACE quality arm -- capture on, five prefill passes
 (off, 10%, 15%, per-layer 10%, off) over the 133-conversation corpus (never
 merge)

Thresholds from measurements/st_ace_routes_20260917: global 10% 0.07012, 15% 0.07679,
per-layer 10% from the same route dump.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 engine/profiles/glm53/boot.py | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/engine/profiles/glm53/boot.py b/engine/profiles/glm53/boot.py
index 86fc8f7a..f3c2e969 100644
--- a/engine/profiles/glm53/boot.py
+++ b/engine/profiles/glm53/boot.py
@@ -107,11 +107,11 @@ TIER_RESERVE_GIB = 16.0             # free space a tier leaves on the filesystem
 # 2026-09-14 hybrid arms were read on (measurements/st_hybrid_head_nll_20260916) and the one #911 said it never ran.
 # A commit that sets it is booted by a fleet hold and fed a corpus through the door; main keeps it False, and with it
 # False nothing here runs. Carried over from the arm branch it was written on, which was never merged.
-EXPERT_CAPTURE = False
+EXPERT_CAPTURE = True   # debug arm (never merge): ACE quality passes
 # A capture arm may feed its corpus several times, one routed-slot skip per pass (capture.Capture skip_passes): a
 # pass is None (every slot served), a normalised-gate threshold, or {layer: threshold}. Empty keeps one pass, no skip.
-ROUTE_SKIP_PASSES = ()
-ROUTE_SKIP_PASS_DOCUMENTS = 0
